<title>USA: Royce Labs gets FDA ok on anti-inflamatory.</title>
<headline>Royce Labs gets FDA ok on anti-inflamatory.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royce Laboratories Inc said Wednesday that it has received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration of its abbreviated new drug application for Etodolac Tablets USP, 400 milligrams.</p>
<p>Etodolac is the generic equivalent of Wyeth Ayerst's Lodine Tablets, which is an anti-inflamatory.</p>
<p>Wyeth Ayerst is a unit of American Home Products Corp.</p>
</text>
